title: Case Manager › Active cases › How a row's status and due pill are decided
route: /manager
intro: Each row's status, step bar, agent line and button come from how far the agents have got. The due pill comes from the kind of request. Both follow the demo clock, so Fast-forward turns 'Notice due in 5 h' into 'Overdue'.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "A draft in 'Being prepared' is drawn"
decision d1 "Is an agent waiting for an answer?"
process a1 "'Needs your input'\nBar stops at 'Ask'\nBadge: the agent who asked (Scribe, or Packet for a recertification)\nLine says what is needed"
decision d2 "Have all ten agents finished?"
process a2 "'Ready to sign'\nBar stops at 'Sign'\nBadge: Integrity\n'Integrity and Scrubber passed. Waiting for a clinician to sign'"
decision d3 "Has the run started?"
process a3 "'Agents working'\nBar follows the next agent: Reader, Verify and Criteria, Historian, Placement and Forecaster, Scribe, Integrity, Packet and Scrubber\nLine, for example: 'Packet is assembling the forms and attachments'"
process a4 "'Intake not finished'\nNo bar step lit\nBadge: Reader\n'Intake is not finished. Add the chart and the payer to start the agents'"
process c1 "Approval chance\nStarts low and climbs while the first six agents finish, then holds\n'Not started' while intake is unfinished"

group gDue "Due pill: which clock the request type starts"
  decision d4 "What type of request?"
  process u1 "Admission: 'Notice due in 5 h'\nRed under 24 h, amber after"
  process u2 "Retro-authorization: 'Window closes in 18 h'\nRed under 24 h, amber after"
  process u3 "Recertification: 'Expires in 3 days'\nAmber under 4 days, grey after"
  process u4 "Continued stay: 'Review due 4:00 pm'\nA time when under a day, a weekday after. Amber"
  process u5 "Initial request: 'Packet due Thu'\nGrey"
  process u6 "Any clock that has passed: 'Overdue' in red"
endgroup

process s2 "The five rows at the start\nR-1042 and I-2207 need input (Scribe, Packet)\nR-0988 is ready to sign\nR-1101 is working (Packet), I-2262 is working (Reader)"
end e1 "Row is drawn with its pills and button"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| a1
d1 -->|No| d2
d2 -->|Yes| a2
d2 -->|No| d3
d3 -->|Yes| a3
d3 -->|No| a4
a1 & a2 & a3 --> c1
a4 --> e1
c1 --> d4
d4 -->|Admission| u1
d4 -->|Retro-authorization| u2
d4 -->|Recertification| u3
d4 -->|Continued stay| u4
d4 -->|Initial request| u5
u1 & u2 & u3 & u4 & u5 -.-> u6
u1 & u2 & u3 & u4 & u5 --> s2
u6 --> s2
s2 --> e1
